# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# TENANT DATA — never commit these.
#
# Every file below can contain real agent names, descriptions, owner object IDs,
# data-source URLs, group identifiers and usage telemetry for a live tenant.
# Running any script in this repository produces them. They are outputs, not
# source, and they belong wherever your organisation keeps tenant data.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Raw exports
agent-builder-inventory.json
agent-builder-details.json
agent-builder-details.selected.json
export-metadata.json

# Analysis outputs
agent-usage-priority.csv
agent-comparison-candidates.csv
agent-purpose-similarity.csv
agent-consolidation-clusters.csv

# Lifecycle and deletion outputs
agent-lifecycle-decisions.csv
agent-block-ledger.csv
agent-block-history.csv
agent-deletion-worklist.csv
raw-audit.csv

# Generated reports
compare-agents-report.md
compare-agents-report.html

# Default and common output directories
Compare-Agents-Export/
export/
Export/
out/
output/

# Belt and braces: anything that looks like an export or a report
*agent-builder-details*.json
*agent-block*.csv
*-worklist.csv
*compare-agents-report*.html

# Every CSV this repository can produce is tenant data, and it ships no CSV of its
# own. Blocking the extension outright also covers custom -CsvPath / -OutputDirectory
# names, which the specific patterns above would miss.
*.csv

# ...except the synthetic test fixtures, which contain no tenant data and are
# required for the regression suite to run on a fresh clone.
!evals/fixtures/
!evals/fixtures/**

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Tooling
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.log
.vscode/
.idea/
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store
